  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Duck Tagine with Pears and Cinnamon",
  "text": "Duck Tagine with Pears and Cinnamon\n\nPreparation time: 10 minutes\n\nCooking time: 60 minutes\n\nYield: 4\n\nIngredients\n\n2 tbsp olive oil,\n\n1 tbsp butter,\n\n2 onions (finely chopped),\n\n5 cm fresh ginger (peeled and finely chopped),\n\n2 cinnamon sticks,\n\na pinch of saffron threads,\n\n1kg boned duck meat,\n\n2 tbsp butter,\n\n4 tbsp dark clear honey,\n\n3 pears (quartered and cubed),\n\n3 tbsp orange flower water,\n\n2 tbsp toasted sesame seeds,\n\nlemon balm leaves (to garnish),\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Heat 2 tbsp of oil and 1 tbsp butter in a tagine over a medium heat.\n\n2. Add the onion and ginger and cook until they start to colour.\n\n3. Add the cinnamon sticks and saffron.\n\n4. Add the duck meat and coat with the ginger and onion.\n\n5. Pour in 600ml water, bring to the boil, then simmer for 40 minutes until the duck is tender.\n\n6. In a separate pan melt 2 tbsp butter.\n\n7. Stir in the honey.\n\n8. Add the pears and cook until they start to caramelize.\n\n9. Add the pears to the tagine.\n\n10. Add the orange flower water and cook for a further 10 minutes.\n\n11. Season, scatter with toasted sesame seeds, and garnish with lemon balm.",
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
  "cookTime": "PT1H",
  "recipeYield": "4",
